# Post-game epilogue arc (QEPI): the Belfry Below. Opens after the ending, when the player continues from the clear.

@scene EPI_BELLWRIGHT
if flag:epi_done done
if q:QEPI:ACTIVE ask
say anse | You heard it too. Last night. Under the sea, once, and wrong.
say anse | That was the Crown's bell. It went down with Veyr. I cast it, when I was an apprentice. I would know its voice anywhere.
say dain | It rang at the fault. It shouldn't ring again.
say anse | Bells don't ring themselves. Something down there is pulling the rope.
say anse | My diving bell still holds air. I'll lower you. I won't come down. I'm old, not stupid.
quest QEPI ACTIVE start
objective dain | Ride Anse's diving bell down to drowned Veyr and find out what is ringing the Crown's bell.
label ask
choice | Go down in the diving bell -> down | Not yet -> wait
label wait
say anse | The sea isn't going anywhere. Neither am I.
end
label down
sfx FX028
fade out 0.8
say narr | The diving bell sinks through green, then grey, then a dark that has weight.
warp EP1_NAVE from_bell up
fade in 0.8
end
label done
say anse | It's quiet down there now. I sleep better. So does the sea.
@end

@scene EPI_ASCEND
choice | Ride the bell back up -> up | Stay below -> stay
label stay
end
label up
fade out 0.6
warp T07_MARKET from_hearth up
fade in 0.6
@end

@scene EPI_NAVE_ALTAR
if flag:epi_keys have
set epi_keys
say narr | The keys are bell-ringers' keys, one for each tower of old Veyr. Someone has kept them polished.
say ilyr | Someone has been waiting for a visitor.
end
label have
say narr | The empty bowl. The altar has nothing more to give.
@end

@scene EPI_BELL1
if flag:epi_b1 rung
set epi_b1
sfx FX029
shake 0.3
say narr | The first bell speaks: low, round, patient. The water in the carillon trembles and settles.
end
label rung
say narr | The first bell hums, still answering.
@end

@scene EPI_BELL2
if flag:epi_b2 rung
if !flag:epi_b1 wrong
set epi_b2
sfx FX029
shake 0.3
say narr | The second bell answers the first. Somewhere above, a grille of bell-metal shifts.
end
label wrong
say narr | The second bell swallows the note before it sounds. It will not speak first.
end
label rung
say narr | The second bell hums, still answering.
@end

@scene EPI_BELL3
if flag:epi_open rung
if !flag:epi_b2 wrong
set epi_b3
set epi_open
sfx FX029
shake 0.8
flash #d8e8ff
say narr | The cracked bell rings last, and right. Three notes hang in the water as one chord. The grille at the top of the stair folds open.
say ilyr | That is the note the Crown's bell was cast to ring. It has forgotten.
end
label wrong
say narr | The cracked bell groans and falls silent. The others have not spoken yet.
end
label rung
say narr | The chord still hangs in the water.
@end

@scene EPI_CARILLON_SHUT
say narr | A grille of bell-metal closes the stair. Three bells wait in the carillon below, each marked with its place in the order.
@end

@scene EPI_BOSS
music silence
say narr | The belfry. The Crown's great bell hangs over nothing, from no rope. It swings anyway.
say dain | No one is pulling it.
say ilyr | It is pulling itself. It rang the fault into the world. It wants to ring it again, and get it right this time.
say narr | The bell turns its mouth toward the party.
battle BX27 noflee
set epi_done
quest QEPI COMPLETED
music M016
say narr | The bell stops swinging. For the first time in a long time, the sea around Veyr is silent.
say ilyr | It rang its last note. The right one.
choice | Leave the bell in the deep -> leave | Raise it for Hearthward -> raise
label leave
set epi_bell_left
say dain | Let it sleep where it fell.
goto after
label raise
set epi_bell_raised
say dain | Anse can hang it in the harbour. Somebody should ring it on purpose.
label after
objective dain | Ride the diving bell back up and tell Anse the sea is quiet.
call EPI_EPILOGUE
@end

@scene EPI_AFTER
say narr | The empty cradle. The water inside the ring does not move.
@end

@scene EPI_EPILOGUE once
say narr | Later, in Hearthward, they tell it around the communal fire, and everyone tells it slightly wrong.
if !flag:epi_bell_raised left
say narr | The Crown's bell hangs in the harbour now. Anse rings it at dawn, badly, and nobody asks him to stop.
goto bell_end
label left
say narr | The Crown's bell stays in the deep. On quiet nights the sailors say they can hear it not ringing.
label bell_end
if !flag:rescue_all nores
say narr | Five names are carved on the lift housing at the Conduit, with the tenders' names beneath: everyone who came up at the last second.
goto res_end
label nores
if !flag:bound_formed res_end
say narr | The Bound still sit together some nights, around a green fire nobody else can see. Nobody asks them to explain. They are still five.
label res_end
if !flag:levelbreak_3 crown
say narr | Far below, in the Hollow Heart, the Unmade Crown stays unmade. The crypts are quiet. The ledger is closed.
label crown
say ilyr | Is it finished?
say dain | No. It's started. That's what we get.
@end
